## Motivation

Falcon-H1's decoder layer calls the Mamba2 backend inline, so a breakable prefill CUDA-graph capture records the Mamba2 extend inside a captured segment. Every replay then reuses the capture-time batch's state slots and chunk metadata rather than the batch being served, with three consequences:

- the request's own Mamba state is never written;
- the first generated token differs from an eager prefill, and on longer prompts the logits are NaN;
- a single server can fault on its first request.

