## Description

On draft step 0 the draft layer runs on every row of the target's verify layout: K+1 rows per generation request and every prompt row of a context chunk. Only one row per request is read afterwards (the workers select it with `hidden_states[gather_ids]` after the layer's forward). The layer's attention must see every row, because it writes the draft KV of each, but everything after it (residual, post-attention norm, MLP / MoE, final norm) is per-token. A draft layer that supports it now runs that post-attention part only on the rows the draft loop reads.

## What does this PR do?

At every durable checkpoint, `RolloutBank.checkpoint()` compacts the bank into a new
generation and clears its writer, expecting the next `set_collection()` call before
any append. The rollout pipeline appends a group whenever it completes one, and its
stages run whenever the trainer runs the event loop:
- when `can_skip_inference()` settles the pipeline at the start of a collection;
- on the skipped-inference path, which never calls `set_collection()`;
- when the inference engine is resumed or suspended, before `set_collection()`;
- during RL evaluation.

